{"schema":1,"function":"chi_ppf","description":"Chi distribution quantile function, the x with P(k/2, x^2/2) = p (k degrees of freedom); sqrt(2 t) with t the gamma quantile","inputs":["k","p"],"outputs":["y"],"points":351,"tolerance":{"rel":2e-13,"reason":"As for gamma_ppf: the quantile is x = sqrt(2 t) with t = exp(L), and rounding L (or 2/k, which multiplies it in the lower tail) to a double changes t by |L| times 2^-53 and x by half that. The largest |L| / 2 = |log(x / sqrt(2))| at a nonzero, normal quantile on this grid is 690.9 (k = 1, p = 1e-300, x = 1.25e-300), so up to 7.7e-14 is unavoidable; 2e-13 allows 2.6x that and matches gamma_ppf. Subnormal quantiles are judged relative to 2.2e-308 (conventions). SciPy's worst error at the points it gets within tolerance is 1.8e-14 (k = 3, p = 1e-300); it fails 4: 0 instead of 1.25e-300 at k = 1, p = 1e-300, and 1.2e-9 to 1.6e-8 off at p = 5e-324 for k >= 300"},"grid":"k in {1, 2, 3, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100, 160, 161, 300, 1e3, 1e4} x the gamma_ppf probabilities p in {0, 5e-324, 1e-300, 1e-100, 1e-50, 1e-20, 1e-10, 1e-5, 1e-3, 0.01, 0.05, 0.1, 0.25, 0.4, 1/2 - 1e-10, 1/2, 1/2 + 1e-10, 0.6, 0.75, 0.9, 0.95, 0.99, 0.999, and the doubles nearest 1 - 1e-5, 1 - 1e-10, 1 - 1e-15, 1}; the quantile is 0 at p = 0 (the end of the support) and p = 1 is tagged pole (+inf)","mpmath":{"version":"1.4.1","dps":[50,100]},"scipy":{"version":"1.18.1","function":"scipy.stats.chi.ppf"},"numpy":"2.5.4","python":"3.13"}
